# Where the toolchain lives.
#
#   cp local.env.example local.env && $EDITOR local.env
#
# Read by the Integration test drivers (test/Integration/).
#
# This file answers "where are the tools". *What* the tests run is a separate,
# optional file: test/Integration/run.env.
#
# `local.env` is git-ignored, so your local paths never get committed.

# --- REQUIRED ----------------------------------------------------------------

# Directory of the ClangIR-enabled clang, together with cir-opt, mlir-opt,
# mlir-translate, opt and llc. Check with: ls $LLVM_BIN/clang $LLVM_BIN/cir-opt
LLVM_BIN="$HOME/llvm-project/build/bin"

# Directory of the built mlir-opt-omp.
OMP_TOOL_BIN="$HOME/mlir-opt-omp/build"

# OpenMP headers used by the clang->CIR front-end. MUST match the GCC installed
# on this machine — find yours with:
#   ls -d /usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/*/include
INC_OMP="/usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/13/include"

# --- Optional (the values shown are the defaults) -----------------------------

# POLYBENCH=""    # PolyBenchC-4.2.1-OpenMP checkout; needed for SUITE=full,
#                 # otherwise the kernels vendored in test/Integration/kernels
# RULES=""        # DSL file; defaults to this repo's rules.dsl
# CLANG="clang"   # override an individual tool by name or path; same for
#                 # GCC, OPT, LLC, CIR_OPT, MLIR_OPT, MLIR_TRANSLATE,
#                 # MLIR_OPT_OMP. Full list and defaults:
#                 # test/Integration/README.md, "Configuration reference".

# --- PULP / gvsoc (only for RUNTIME=pmsis) ------------------------------------

# PULP_APP_DIR="$HOME/PolyBench-PULP"   # harness dir with the PULP-SDK Makefile
# PULP_SDK_ENV="$HOME/gap_sdk/configs/gap8_v3.sh"   # sourced automatically
# PULP_TOOLCHAIN_BIN="$HOME/toolchains/gap_riscv_toolchain/INSTALL/bin"

# riscv32-capable opt/llc with the xpulpv backend — often a different LLVM
# install than LLVM_BIN above. Default: the host opt/llc.
# PULP_OPT="$HOME/toolchains/llvm-riscv/bin/opt"
# PULP_LLC="$HOME/toolchains/llvm-riscv/bin/llc"
